# Onboard Specs

Convert `project-specs.md` into factory artifacts. Do not implement source.

## Preconditions

- `.factory/AGENTS.md` exists (initialize the submodule if needed).
- `project-specs.md` is the source specification.
- Working tree is clean enough that artifact-only edits are reviewable.

## Allocate IDs first

```bash
git fetch --all --prune
factory ids next REQ DES ARCH DEC TASK --all-refs
```

Use only numbers this command returns. Re-run the same command immediately before any push that adds artifacts.

## Read

- `project-specs.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `.factory/AGENTS.md`
- `.factory/docs/artifact-model.md`, `.factory/docs/project-discovery.md`, `.factory/docs/task-lifecycle.md`
- Templates under `.factory/templates/` for each artifact type you will write

Do not invent facts that are not in the spec or repository files. Preserve `Approved` / `Preferred` / `Proposed` / `Unknown` wording. Mark commands and stack as expected or proposed when source does not yet exist.

## Write

- `vision.md` — problem, goals, non-goals
- `project.md` — domain, actors, modules, constraints, declared stack
- `roadmap.md` — MVP and priority bands
- `.factory-state/artifacts/DISC-0001-project-context.md` — update, do not duplicate
- `REQ-xxxx-*.md` for features and acceptance criteria
- `DES-xxxx-*.md` only when the spec describes UX, screens, flows, or developer-facing experience
- `ARCH-xxxx-*.md` or `DEC-xxxx-*.md` only when the spec states architecture, data, integrations, or deployment
- Tasks under `.factory-state/tasks/backlog/` unless scope, inputs, outputs, dependencies, acceptance criteria, and validation are all clear — those go in `todo/`

Each task must link the artifacts it depends on. Keep `TASK-0001` updated or move it forward when discovery is represented elsewhere.

## After

Summarize files created and updated, assumptions, open questions, and the recommended next task. Run `factory ready` and report remaining gaps. Do not scaffold, install dependencies, or write application source.
